ber>7016943</doc-number> <kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations> <non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1172202A1</text> <sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ANZAI MITSURU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITADA ICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KUREHA CHEMICAL IND CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOBITA HISANORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ANZAI, MITSURU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITADA, ICHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUREHA KAGAKU KOGYO KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOBITA, HISANORI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ANZAI MITSURU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITADA ICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOBITA HISANORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ANZAI, MITSURU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITADA, ICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOBITA, HISANORI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A multilayered casing film which comprises at least three layers consisting of two polyamide layers and an adhesive polyolefin layer disposed therebetween. At least one of the polyamide layers comprises a polyamide homopolymer and has a higher melting point and a smaller thickness than the other polyamide layer. The adhesive polyolefin layer is in direct contact with at least one of the polyamide layers and is formed from an acid-modified  alpha -olefin resin. The multilayered casing film is excellent in stretchability, thermal shrinkability, shearing processability, etc., and is capable of stable film formation by the inflation method. It further has improved high-temperature creep resistance and excellent thermal stability during molding, which have conventionally been difficult to satisfy simultaneously. It is especially suitable as a packaging material for foods such as ham and sausage.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un film à boyau multicouche comprenant au moins trois couches, dont deux couches de polyamide séparées par une couche de polyoléfine adhésive. L'une au moins des couches de polyamide, qui comprend un homopolymère polyamide, se caractérise par un point de fusion plus élevée et une épaisseur plus faible que l'autre couche polyamide. La couche de polyoléfine adhésive se trouve en contact direct avec au moins une des couches polyamides et est constituée par une résine d' alpha -oléfine modifiée acide. Le film à boyau présente de remarquables caractéristiques en termes d'étirabilité, de thermorétrécissabilité, de résistance au cisaillement, etc., et se prête à une formation stable par gonflage. De plus, ce film présente une résistance accrue au fluage sous haute température et une excellente stabilité thermique au moulage, qualités qu'il était jusqu'à présent difficile d'obtenir simultanément. Ce film à boyau convient tout particulièrement pour l'emballage de denrées alimentaires telles que jambon ou saucisses.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>